                <pb facs="0604" n="600" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg600"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.00/790: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-26T20:00:00+09:00">May 26, 1938—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 26—7:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>332. It has just been announced that following Cabinet appointments were made
                    this afternoon: Foreign Affairs, General Ugaki; Finance and Commerce and
                    Industry, Seishin Ikeda; Education, General Araki. Comment follows.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
